# Linting

Every code change MUST be linted before the task is complete.

## Required Steps

1. Identify the project's linter from config files (`eslint.config.*`, `.eslintrc*`, `biome.json`, `golangci.yml`, `ruff.toml`, etc.).
2. Run the linter on **all files you created or modified**.
3. Fix every error and warning the linter reports for those files.
4. If the project has a formatter (`prettier`, `biome format`, `gofmt`), run it on changed files.

## Preferred Commands (use what the repo defines)

```bash
# After tooling is set up — adjust to match package.json / Makefile / CI
npm run lint          # or: pnpm lint, bun run lint
npm run format        # if separate from lint
```

If no lint script exists yet, set one up as part of the first implementation task and document the command in the project README.

## Do Not

- Disable lint rules inline (`eslint-disable`, `//nolint`) without a one-line justification for non-obvious cases.
- Commit code with linter errors in changed files.
- Assume CI will catch issues — verify locally first.

## Completion Signal

In the task summary, state which lint command was run and that it passed on changed files.
